  - name: MAHTEP Group, Politecnico di Torino
    website: 'http://www.mahtep.polito.it/'
abstract: >-
  A single-region (OECD Europe) model instance for the optimization of the
  European energy system up to 2050, developed within an extended version of
  the TEMOA (Tools for Energy Modeling Optimization and Analysis) modeling
  framework, in an open-source and open-data environment.
repository-code: 'https://github.com/MAHTEP/TEMOA-Europe'
url: 'http://www.mahtep.polito.it/'
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - energy system optimization
  - energy planning
  - TEMOA
  - Europe
  - European Green Deal
  - net-zero emissions by 2050
  - open source
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    TEMOA-europe: An open-source and open-data energy system optimization
    model for the analysis of the European energy mix
  authors:
    - given-names: Daniele
      family-names: Lerede
    - given-names: Valeria
      family-names: Di Cosmo
    - given-names: Laura
      family-names: Savoldi
  journal: Energy
  volume: 308
  number: 132850
  year: 2024
  month: 11
  issn: 0360-5442
  publisher:
    name: Elsevier
  doi: 10.1016/j.energy.2024.132850
